  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently the Upright parameter is driven by head position. When using a prone animation with tracking control on the head set to animation, you are unable to leave the prone state as the head can no longer move out of the animation.\n\nTo put it simply, you cant animate your head at all when prone, or else you will be stuck in the prone state.\n\nA possible suggestion to resolve this would to base the upright parameter on camera height rather than head position.",
